// scripts/rb1g-self-closeout.mjs
//
// RB-1G self-validation closeout（repair round）— the card's OWN bundle is
// generated by the PRODUCTION mandatory closeout hook（runMandatoryGraphCloseout
// → runCloseoutGate → generate → pre-write secret scan → atomic write →
// independent validation）, the same hook the generic Graph runner
//（runColimaGraph）calls at card closeout. No hand-written bundle, no manual
// CLI generation for the card itself.
//
// If a previous RB-1G delivery record exists in OUT, this run is a REPAIR
// generation: the new bundle explicitly SUPERSEDES the previous bundle
//（new identity + new sha256; old artifact retained, never overwritten）and
// records the repair attempt history. The superseded bundle is the CHAIN
// HEAD（the newest record no other record supersedes）— never a stale one.
//
// RB-1G's own rule（the card must obey its own governance）:
//   1. Internal Review/Repair Graph completed            -> this run
//   2. RB-1G review bundle auto-generated                -> closeout hook
//   3. Bundle validator PASS                             -> independent validator
//   4. Bundle provided to the external reviewer          -> sender may record at
//      most a NON-AUTHORITATIVE delivery attempt
//   5. External reviewer ACTUALLY reads the bundle       -> reviewer reads it
//   6. External reviewer declares final PASS/REPAIR/HOLD -> --apply-verdict
//      （the verdict IS the receipt: RECEIVED + REVIEWED proven in one step）
//
// Until step 5/6 happen the honest ceiling is:
//   HOLD / AWAITING_EXTERNAL_REVIEW_BUNDLE_DELIVERY
// （externalReviewStatus AWAITING_EXTERNAL_REVIEW; externalReviewComplete=false
// — never EXTERNAL_REVIEW_PASS / CARD_COMPLETE; no sender-side confirmed flag）.
//
// Run: node scripts/rb1g-self-closeout.mjs

